<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Strike hits South Africa's Chromebronne mine.</title>
<headline>Strike hits South Africa's Chromebronne mine.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's National Union of Mineworkers (NUM) said on Tuesday 1,000 staff at the Chromebronne Mining Division and Cashane Plant were on strike.</p>
<p>The strike, which began on Monday night, follows a failure to reach agreement with management on wages and working conditions, the NUM said.</p>
<p>The NUM wants a 12-15 percent rise, while management has offered nine to 10 percent.</p>
<p>Strikers also want a change in the implementation date for annual wage rises and an end to the current job grading system, the union said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
